# The kernel's view of several virtual memories per copy (Inputs/vmem_multi:
# per leaf, four byte lanes of one RAM, a RAM written at their address and read
# there, one read elsewhere, 32 x 16 and 8 x 26 RAMs; two copies of two leaves).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/Inputs/vmem_multi
# Apart, a controller each: 8 memories a copy, a region each.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --copies Leaf:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLAIN < %t/plain/foldsim_sim.vh
# PLAIN: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 16
# PLAIN: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_DW 8
# PLAIN-NOT: GROUP
# PLAIN: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_BYTES 64'h10000
# --vmem-merge-lanes: the lanes, and the RAM read and written at their
# addresses (their read-address registers always agree), are one memory of five
# byte lanes, a byte enable each; the RAM read elsewhere stays apart.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/merged --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-merge-lanes --copies Leaf:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MERGED < %t/merged/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MERGEDJ < %t/merged/foldsim_sim.json
# MERGED: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 8
# MERGED-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_IW 1
# MERGED-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_AW 4
# MERGED-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_DW 40
# MERGED-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_MW 5
# MERGED: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_DW 8
# MERGED-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_MW 1
# MERGEDJ: "memory": "g_lane_0.lane/Memory_x5"
# MERGEDJ: "memory": "pair1/Memory"
# MERGEDJ: "memory": "m16/Memory"
# MERGEDJ: "memory": "m26/Memory"
# --vmem-group copy: a controller per copy, its members placed largest first
# (m16's 32 rows, the lanes' 16, pair1's 16, m26's 8: rows 0, 32, 48, 64 of a
# 128-row image of 40-bit rows with byte enables); each member's base is its
# image's in the vmem space, the group's region 4 KiB aligned.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/group --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-merge-lanes --vmem-group copy --copies Leaf:2 Leaf 2> %t/group.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GROUP < %t/group/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GROUPJ < %t/group/foldsim_sim.json
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GROUPL < %t/group.log
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 8
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_BASE 64'h1000
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_GROUP 0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_GROW 32
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_GROUP 0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_GROW 48
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_2_BASE 64'h0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_2_GROUP 0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_2_GROW 0
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_3_GROUP 0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_3_GROW 64
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_4_GROUP 1
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_GROUPS 2
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_N 4
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_IW 1
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_AW 7
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_DW 40
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_MW 5
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_INSTANCES 2
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_RDWRF 0
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_BASE 64'h0
# GROUP: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_BASE 64'h3000
# GROUP-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_BYTES 64'h6000
# GROUPJ: "group_row": 32,
# GROUPJ-NEXT: "group": 0,
# GROUPJ-NEXT: "group_member": 0
# GROUPJ: "vmem_groups": [
# GROUPJ: "members": [
# GROUPJ-NEXT: 0,
# GROUPJ-NEXT: 1,
# GROUPJ-NEXT: 2,
# GROUPJ-NEXT: 3
# GROUPL: foldsim: vmem controllers: g0 vm0+vm1+vm2+vm3, g1 vm4+vm5+vm6+vm7
# At most N members a controller; with --vmem-cache-rows, each controller's
# lines (FOLDSIM_VMEM_G<g>_CACHE_ROWS) over all its members' rows.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/three --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-merge-lanes --vmem-group 3 --vmem-cache-rows 64 --copies Leaf:2 Leaf 2> %t/three.log > /dev/null
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=THREE < %t/three/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=THREEL < %t/three.log
# THREE: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_GROUPS 4
# THREE-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_N 3
# THREE: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G0_CACHE_ROWS 64
# THREE: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_N 1
# THREE-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_IW 1
# THREE-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_AW 3
# THREE-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_DW 32
# THREE-NEXT: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_MW 1
# THREE: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_G1_CACHE_ROWS 16
# THREEL: foldsim: vmem controllers: g0 vm0+vm1+vm2 64 lines, g1 vm3 16 lines, g2 vm4+vm5+vm6 64 lines, g3 vm7 16 lines
# Without the options the output is as before (the simulator's ports never
# depend on them).
# RUN: sed -e 's#%t/plain/##g' %t/plain/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/plain.sv
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/plain2 --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-group copy --copies Leaf:2 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: sed -e 's#%t/plain2/##g' %t/plain2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/plain2.sv
# RUN: cmp %t/plain.sv %t/plain2.sv
# Errors, before anything is compiled.
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bad --static --vmem-group copy Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOVM
# NOVM: --vmem-group needs --virtual-memories
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bad --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-group 0 Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bad --static --virtual-memories 'Leaf:.*' --vmem-group all Leaf 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
# BAD: --vmem-group: copy, or the memories per controller (at least 1)
